@startuml single-signal-path
title US-06: Single Signal Path - Only One Weak Signal Present, No Composite Raised

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

participant "Alert\nEvaluator\n(leader)" as Evaluator
database "Redis\nalert-state:{id}\n(hash)" as AlertState
database "Redis\nrecent-loss:{id}\n(hash)" as RecentLoss
queue "Kafka\nproximity.candidates" as ProxKafka
queue "Kafka\nalerts" as Kafka

== Signal loss only - no proximity candidate arrives within window ==

note over Evaluator
  Signal loss detected via scheduled Redis scan.
  HSET alert-state:VesselB { dark_since_ms, signal_loss_alert_id }.
  SIGNAL_LOSS alert emitted immediately.
  No proximity.candidates event has arrived
  for VesselB within COMPOSITE_CORRELATION_WINDOW_MS.
  Only one weak signal present.
  SIGNAL_LOSS remains active — no supersession.
end note

Evaluator -> Kafka : publish SIGNAL_LOSS alert immediately\n{ alert_id, alert_type: SIGNAL_LOSS, entity_id: VesselB,\n  dark_since_ms }

== Proximity candidate arrives - no active or recent signal loss ==

ProxKafka -> Evaluator : consume proximity.candidates event\n{ pair_key, entity_a_id: VesselC, entity_b_id: VesselD,\n  episode_start_ms, timestamp_ms, lat, lon, distance_at_detection }

Evaluator -> AlertState : HGETALL alert-state:VesselC
AlertState --> Evaluator : nil — no active signal loss for VesselC

Evaluator -> AlertState : HGETALL alert-state:VesselD
AlertState --> Evaluator : nil — no active signal loss for VesselD

Evaluator -> RecentLoss : HGETALL recent-loss:VesselC
RecentLoss --> Evaluator : nil — not recently dark

Evaluator -> RecentLoss : HGETALL recent-loss:VesselD
RecentLoss --> Evaluator : nil — not recently dark

note over Evaluator
  VesselC and VesselD are in proximity
  but neither has gone dark (active or recently).
  No signal loss component.
  Only one weak signal present.
  No composite alert raised.
  Emit UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY only.
end note

Evaluator -> Kafka : publish UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY alert\n{ alert_id, alert_type: UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY,\n  pair_key, episode_start_ms,\n  entity_c, entity_d, distance_at_detection }

note over Kafka
  Composite alert requires BOTH:
  signal loss AND unscheduled proximity
  within COMPOSITE_CORRELATION_WINDOW_MS.
  Neither case above qualifies for supersession.
end note

@enduml
